{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report — fix landed and merged\n\n**Status:** Code fix MERGED via Gerrit change 2438; ticket closed `preexisting`,\ncaused_by `786b-190d-5e3a-4194`. Live-validation AC deferred to operator edge-deploy (see the\n`[non-codebase]` disposition comment above); non-blocking.\n\n**Root cause (proven).** `location /review/` proxies with a prefix-STRIPPING\n`proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}/;`, so the review-bot never sees `/review/`.\nIts only absolute redirects are Starlette slash-307s to its own routes, built from the public\n`Host` header — so post-a61d it emits `https://$host/<route>` with no `/review/` to strip, and\nthe prefix is lost (→ 404 on Gerrit fallthrough). Confirmed on real nginx 1.27-alpine + a stub\nupstream: current block loses the prefix; block + the one new rule restores it; both leave the\nprefix-stripping REQUEST path (`GET /review/health` → app `/health`) unchanged, and a61d's\nhttp→https scheme guarantee intact.\n\n**Fix (Option 1, edge-only).** One per-location rule appended to the `/review/` block AFTER\na61d's scheme backstops (`proxy_redirect default;` stays first):\n`proxy_redirect https://$host/ https://$host/review/;`. nginx applies the first MATCHING\nredirect; this rule's `https://$host/` LHS overlaps none of a61d's `http://…` rules, so ordering\nis safe and both a61d's scheme guarantee and the prefix-stripping request path are preserved.\nA guard comment documents the same-app-only precondition + the broad-rewrite residual. No app\nchange (Option 2 rejected per 2026-08-30 decision).\n\n**RED→GREEN.** 4 structural tests over the RENDERED config (reuse a61d's `_render_nginx()`):\n(1) redirect Location retains `/review/`; (2) request path stays prefix-stripping; (3) a61d\nscheme + default-first ordering intact; (4) review-bot redirect surface pinned same-app-only.\nThe two behaviour tests were legitimately RED before the rule (held out from the fixer);\nsandboxed mutation check: delete the rule → RED, misorder `default` → RED, restore → GREEN.\n\n**Gates:** plan-review certified; LLM-Review +1; Verified +1; completion-verifier signed.\n\n**Parity sweep.** `/review/` is the ONLY prefix-stripping surface where external prefix ≠ app\ninternal path. `/opcert/` (no trailing slash, prefix preserved, guard-gated fail-closed),\n`/mcp` (external==internal), Gerrit `/` — none can emit a prefix-losing redirect. No sibling\ntickets needed.\n\n**Residual (bounded).** A future off-`/review/` same-host absolute redirect would be wrongly\nprefixed by the broad rewrite; bounded by the guard comment + the same-app-only test (turns RED\nif the app ever grows such a redirect)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788114703454512001,"uuid":"bc05e298-9f67-4abe-8845-68456f9ac0b9"}